Expected elements: present

Every §4 must-show item is present and legible: nav with resolver, the affirmative `Real Aztec mainnet data` banner with slug and producer sentences, breadcrumb, full hash plus `Succeeded`, the `Not observable` badge with the published pruning reason, Overview with block/canonicality/finality/cost, all six sections in permanent tense, the provenance strip with all three marks drawn, the correct footer disclosure. Nothing forbidden. Typographically the page reads as correct rather than broken: four clean levels (≈35 px mono title / 24 px section heads / 15 px body at 22 px leading / 12 px tracked caps labels), mono confined to values.

Findings. The two worst are in the Overview cost row: the value is a 32-byte hex word with ~50 leading zeros set unbroken, so the magnitude is unreadable and the meaningful digits sit at the far right edge of the cell — while the title and breadcrumb elide hashes; and its label, the adapter's camelCase field uppercased to `TRANSACTIONFEE`, loses its only word boundary, wraps, and doubles that row's height. The footer disclosure runs ~129 characters per line where every other paragraph is capped near 85. In the `Not observable` card, paragraph leading is 25 px against a 22 px line, so the published reason — the page's whole point — is typographically indistinguishable from the framing sentence above it.

Highest-priority fixes: format the fee as a quantity (or elide it like every other hash) and de-camelCase the label; give the reason paragraph real separation.

Rating: 6/10

